WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
Pick any atom.

2
00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.420
Now blow it up until it's
as wide as a sports stadium.

3
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.580
The electrons are spread out around it,
held in by the nucleus at the very middle.

4
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.710
On that scale, how big is the nucleus?

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.830
Something you could pick up, or
something that fills the stadium?

6
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.900
In this mission, you'll
look inside the nucleus,

7
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.210
at its protons and neutrons.

8
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:28.350
Each has about 1840 times
the mass of an electron.

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.390
So where does an atom keep its mass?

10
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:35.290
Then you'll compare the width of an
atom with the width of its nucleus,

11
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.880
in powers of ten.

12
00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:42.090
Your mission: estimate how big the nucleus
would be at the middle of a stadium-sized

13
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:42.840
atom.
